Yep — the spaces are being collapsed because each letter is in its own span.

Replace this line:

characterElement.textContent = character;

with this:

characterElement.textContent = character === " " ? "\u00A0" : character;

That restores the visible spaces between words.

is this coded or is it in an mp3? 

That specific screen is almost certainly just an image being displayed by the answer page — not something generated from MP3 audio.

In your script, Answer pages work like this:

variant = "plain"
image = ""
audio = ""

Then later:

<img src="${esc(image)}">

So the large yellow “h” screen is probably:

    a static PNG/JPG

    assigned as the image

    shown by the generic answer renderer

The MP3 only plays if:

hasAudio = Boolean(audio)

and an audio file path exists.

So:

    visuals = coded/displayed via image path

    sound = optional MP3 layer on top

Not embedded in the MP3 itself.

